# Testing (AUnit)

**Every implemented feature must have tests.** Use **AUnit** ([AdaCore/aunit](https://github.com/AdaCore/aunit)) for all Ada tests. This is an allowed third-party library.

- Add tests in the same change as the feature; do not ship untested compiler/JIT/LIR/CLI/`tooling`/`hypatia`/`alexandria`/`format` behavior.
- Prefer AUnit fixtures/test cases over ad-hoc `Put_Line` drivers. Samples under `samples/<feature>/` are extra, not a substitute for unit tests (see samples rule).
- Host tests live in a **nested Alire crate** (`<folder>/tests`, own `alire.toml`, pin `{ path = ".." }`, crate name `lovelace_<component>_tests`). Declare AUnit **only** there, not on the library or `lovelace` crates. Host test crates `with` `shared/lovelace_host_switches.gpr` and include `shared/test_status/` for `Lovelace.Test_Status` (cyan suite header + colored `NAME [OK|FAIL|INCONCLUSIVE]` reporter).
- Host crates (full RTS): AUnit with file I/O is fine.
- Freestanding/native Augusta Ada: AUnit is designed for **ZFP**. In that code, do **not** use containers, finalization, or exception propagation even in tests. Honor AUnit `FileIO` vs `nofileio` as needed.
- Optional CLI integration tests (`lovelace/integration_tests`): require `wasm-tools` and `wasmtime` on `PATH`, validate every generated `.wasm`/`.wat`, and **run** only entrypoint programs (see [integration-tests.mdc](integration-tests.mdc)).
- `scripts/run-tests.ps1` builds quietly (`alr … *> $null`, log shown only on build failure), then runs each test binary so output is status lines only.

Do not pull other test frameworks (VUnit, Python pytest for Ada units, etc.) unless the user asks.